Subject: [PATCH] nft-fullcone: manage its dedicated RCU destruction hook

Keep ctnetlink's callback untouched. Publish one FullCone callback per
network namespace while rules exist, using the existing lifecycle mutex
and per-netns rule count. Clear only our own callback on the last rule,
and wait for in-flight RCU readers before releasing resources.

Allocate the workqueue before publishing expressions and unwind failed
initialization. The kernel invokes the callback once per confirmed UDP
connection, independently of Netlink retries and event cache allocation.

---
--- a/src/nft_ext_fullcone.c
+++ b/src/nft_ext_fullcone.c
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
 #include <linux/netfilter/nf_tables.h>
 #include <net/netfilter/nf_tables.h>
 #include <net/netfilter/nf_nat.h>
+#include <net/netns/generic.h>
 
 #include <linux/workqueue.h>
 
